      ":question/id": "2a127128-cb22-56be-ba7d-5b1447ce81f1",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-139957",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $a\\cdot (a+b)=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $a\\cdot a<0$ is false. Indeed, $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement $b\\cdot a>0$ and $b\\cdot a=5$ are false. Simplifying the expression $a\\cdot (a+b)=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (a+b) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $b\\cdot a<0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"."
    }
