      ":question/id": "a61d7528-3ce2-5d0a-af23-11395074997a",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131723",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=3 \\\\ -3x+3y-3z &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 19\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=19,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is inconsistent” is true."
    }
